{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310772,"nonce":"bQvPfGHEL8xnPe/LvN7NsLyP6zs=","title":"Macros can now read custom annotations via EMeta reification; the read path works but only when the annotation is the outermost node, and ...","message":"**READ PATH WORKS END TO END.** A macro author can define a custom annotation\nand act on it:\n\n```haxe\nmacro static function nameOf(e:haxe.macro.Expr):haxe.macro.Expr {\n    switch (e.expr) {\n        case EMeta(s, inner): return macro $v{s.name};   // s.params too\n        case _: return macro \"none\";\n    }\n}\nAnn.nameOf(@:mine 1)          // -\u003e \"mine\"\nAnn.arity(@:tag(\"a\",\"b\") 1)   // -\u003e 2\n```\n\n**What was missing:** `expr_kind_to_value` (`macro_system/ast_bridge.rs`) reifies\n`ExprKind` into pattern-matchable `Enum(\"ExprDef\", ...)` values, and only ~6 of\n~50 variants were covered. `Meta` fell to a catch-all that wraps the node as an\nOPAQUE `MacroValue::Expr`, which `case EMeta(s, e):` can never match. Added an\narm producing:\n\n```\nEnum(\"ExprDef\", \"EMeta\", [\n  Object{ name: String, params: Array\u003cExpr\u003e, pos: Position },   // MetadataEntry\n  Expr,                                                          // annotated expr\n])\n```\n\nConventions to keep: children are wrapped ONE LEVEL as `MacroValue::Expr`, never\nrecursively reified (mirrors the `ECall` arm) — a macro descends by reading\n`.expr` again. ExprDef uses `MacroValue::Enum`, NOT the `Object{kind,__args__}`\nencoding that `ComplexType`/`FieldType` use.\n\n**DELIBERATE DEVIATION:** Haxe declares `?params`; we always emit an array,\nempty when absent. Macro code must test `s.params.length == 0`, not\n`s.params != null`. Matches what field metadata already does.\n\n**MEASURED LIMITS (all asserted in the oracle so they stay visible):**\n- **The annotation must be the OUTERMOST node of the macro's argument.**\n  `Ann.nameOf((@:mine 1))` returns \"none\" — `EParenthesis` is unreified so the\n  walk stops at an opaque Expr. Same for EIf, EArrayDecl, EVars, etc.\n- **`@foo` and `@:foo` are INDISTINGUISHABLE.** Both parsers drop the colon, so\n  `name` is \"foo\" either way. The four `strip_prefix(':')` sites in the compiler\n  are defensive no-ops. Prepending the colon to match Haxe would break every\n  direct `m.name == \"native\"` comparison — needs a separate additive field, not\n  a rename.\n- **Construction is impossible.** `return EMeta(s, inner)` fails E0100;\n  `macro @:mine $e{e}` fails E0200 (reification does not descend Meta).\n  `value_to_expr`'s Enum arm emits `EnumName.Variant(args)` as a field-access\n  call, not a reconstructed AST node.\n- A macro CALL under metadata (`@:tag M.id(4)`) never expands.\n\nOracle: `compiler/tests/haxe/test_macro_annotation.hx`.\n**Run macro tests with `--no-cache`** — a fresh `RAYZOR_CACHE_DIR` still skips\nthe compile and everything looks inert.\n\nRelated: [[feature_expression_metadata_rd_parser]] (the parser half).\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `feature_macro_custom_annotations` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}